abstract: >-
  heav3ns-censor is a deterministic, cryptographically verifiable Rust image post-processing
  engine designed for localized Japanese-style obscuration (Article 175 mosaic, kuro-nuri /
  shiro-nuri graphic bars, and halo-padded separable Gaussian blur) over inverse-rotated
  Signed Distance Field (SDF) primitives (Rect, Ellipse, and Pill capsule). It guarantees
  100% bit-exact preservation of all pixels outside the localized masks while verifying
  both mean and 95th-percentile peak gradient suppression across native resolution, 1080p
  (Q85 JPEG), and 540p (Q75 JPEG) downscaling.

